# ============================================================================
# Git attributes
#
# Purpose:       Controls how Git normalizes line endings for every file in the
#                repository.
# Role:          Every script, env file and config in this repository is
#                bind-mounted into Linux containers. Windows-style CRLF line
#                endings break shell scripts ("bad interpreter") and add a
#                trailing \r to env values, so all files are forced to LF.
# Prerequisites: None. Applies automatically on checkout. After changing this
#                file on an existing clone, run `git add --renormalize .` to
#                re-apply it to files already checked out.
# Variables:     None.
# ============================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line ending normalization
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# text=auto  let Git detect text files (binary files are left untouched)
# eol=lf     always check text files out with LF, even on Windows
* text=auto eol=lf
